gram responsiveness and the association with resident wellness. J Surg Educ. 2022;79(6):e1-e11. doi: 10.1016/j.jsurg.2022.05.004 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Foote DC, Donkersloot JN, Sandhu G, Ziegler K, Lau J. Identifying institutional factors in general surgery resident wellness and burnout. Am J Surg. 2022;223(1):53-57. doi: 10.1016/j.amjsurg.2021.07.014 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Hartzband P, Groopman J. Physician burnout, interrupted. N Engl J Med. 2020;382(26):2485-2487. doi: 10.1056/NEJMp2003149 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Bongiovanni T, Yeo H, Sosa JA, et al. Attrition from surgical residency training: perspectives from those who left. Am J Surg. 2015;210(4):648-654. doi: 10.1016/j.amjsurg.2015.05.014 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Freeman RB, Medoff JL. What Do Unions Do? Basic Books; 1984. [ Google Scholar ] 22. Khoushhal Z, Hussain MA, Greco E, et al. Prevalence and causes of attrition among surgical residents: a systematic review and meta-analysis. JAMA Surg. 2017;152(3):265-272. doi: 10.1001/jamasurg.2016.4086 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Karns JE. The National Labor Relations Board redefines “medical employee” under the Wagner Act regarding residents and interns thereby opening the door to unionization and collective bargaining demands. Spec Law Dig Health Care Law. 2003;(286):9-26. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Rosenbaum L. What do trainees want? The rise of house staff unions. N Engl J Med. 2024;390(3):279-283. doi: 10.1056/NEJMms2308224 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Hilker S, Butler A. Valuing the resident physician: advocating for change. NEJM Resid 360. May 10, 2023. Accessed December 4, 2023. https://resident360.nejm.org/expert-consult/valuing-the-resident-physician-advocating-for-change# [ Google Scholar ] 26. Morrissey PJ, Dworkin MS, Quinn MS. Impact of inflation on real resident wages. Acad Med. 2023;98(11):1237-1238. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0000000000005353 [ DOI ] [